From: lavachemist <48248311+lavachemist@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8550: no IPA firmware memory-region

Linux 7.3 points the (disabled) IPA node at the ipa_fw_mem reserved
region. ROCKNIX's sm8550 device trees delete that region to give the memory
back (pb-os has no modem), which leaves a dangling phandle and dtc
refuses to build them. Drop the reference again, as in 7.2.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
index d60b1570bf39..4be8d4f1ba37 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
@@ -3110,7 +3110,6 @@ &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS>,
 						"ipa-clock-enabled";
 
 			qcom,gsi-loader = "self";
-			memory-region = <&ipa_fw_mem>;
 			sram = <&ipa_modem_tables>;
 
 			status = "disabled";
